  "section_notes": "S2 sets a permanent 8% thermal-test failure limit with no automatic sales stop and open-ended risk-based restrictions, while requiring private numerical disclosure to purchasers and confidentiality from the public. S3 delays new-unit remote shut-off until 36 months and allows a 72-month retrofit deadline with an infeasibility escape. S5 makes recall mandatory at 8 incidents/100k, which strongly favors Northwind (Hearth 10 at 6.4) and burdens Halcyon (Ember 8 at 9.9); S1 and S4 are relatively strict but within acceptable bounds."
